# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: VCMI.
Package: VCMI
Section: Games
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Suggests: GOGImport
Components: Apps.Games.!VCMI (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-vcmi
Description: Open-source engine for Heroes of Might and Magic III
 VCMI 1.7.5 plays Heroes of Might and Magic III (Shadow of Death and
 Complete) in a desktop window or full screen. It needs the files from
 your own copy of the game (GOG.com or CD); GOGImport gets them out of
 the GOG installer. ARMv7 with VFP; a Raspberry Pi 4 is recommended.
Build-Map: !VCMI -> Apps/Games/!VCMI
Build-Notice: VCMI, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-vcmi/releases
 .
 VCMI 1.7.5 (vcmi.eu) and the RISC OS changes are under the GNU GPL
 version 2 or later; FuzzyLite is GPL version 3, so the program as a
 whole is passed on under the GPL version 3. The libraries keep their
 own licences. Heroes of Might and Magic is a trademark of Ubisoft;
 none of the game's files are included. Licences follow.
Build-Copyright: !VCMI/docs/COPYING
Build-Copyright: !VCMI/docs/Licences
Build-Copyright: !VCMI/docs/PThreadTicker-Licence
